# Testing Rules

## Test Credentials

```
Email: test.employe.1@gmail.com
Pass:  admin@123
```

## Mandatory Test Flow

### 1. Auth Verification
- Login succeeds with valid credentials
- Login fails gracefully with invalid credentials

### 2. CRUD Happy Path
```
Create → Read → Update → Delete → Refresh (data persists correctly?)
```

### 3. Error Scenarios

| Input | Expected Result |
|-------|----------------|
| Empty required field | Validation error message |
| Wrong format | Helpful error |
| Expired token | Redirect to login |
| Unauthorized action | 403 + permission message |
| Large payload | Rejection with error |

### 4. Edge Cases
- Empty states — no data exists
- Min/max values — boundaries respected
- Special characters and emojis — no breakage
- Rapid double-click — debounced or disabled
- Refresh mid-mutation — state consistent
- Slow network — loading states visible

### 5. Security
- User sees only their organization's data
- Cross-org access blocked
- Role permissions enforced

### 6. UI States
- Loading indicator visible during data fetch
- Error message displayed on failure
- Empty state shown when no data
- Success feedback after mutation
- Form disabled during submit

## API Test Template

```bash
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8085/api/v1/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"test.employe.1@gmail.com","password":"admin@123"}' \
  | jq -r '.accessToken')

curl -s http://localhost:8085/api/v1/[endpoint] \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | jq
```

## Before Closing

- No `console.log` in code
- No debug/test code committed
- No hardcoded test data in production code
- No dev shortcuts or workarounds
